+# TLS backend
+
+The project's recorded decision is to use rustls as its TLS backend, chosen as a pure Rust implementation that avoids the CVE exposure of the previous choice. Certificate verification stays enabled on all builds, including development, and HTTPS is enforced everywhere with no plaintext exception, even for internal services.
